{
 "id": "20-02-trim-the-multiplier",
 "title": "Trim the 4x4 multiplier to 64 gates",
 "kind": "logic",
 "story": "A 4x4 array multiplier makes 16 partial products with AND gates and adds them with 12 full adders (5 gates each): 76 gates. In four of those adders one input is always 0, so a half adder (2 gates) would do. Four of those adders have their last three gates (sum XOR, carry-through AND, carry-out OR) left open, and two other adders have their sum and carry-through gates left open: slots S1-S16. Which adders really have a constant 0 input? Fill every slot with a gate or with a plain wire (a wire passes its first input through and costs nothing) so that all 256 products are right with at most 64 gates.",
